# AL-2 implementation findings

Status: implementation complete; laptop JVM quick gates green.
Node, Dart and slow-tier gates remain for the orchestrator on shiva.
No git write commands used. No open implementation/design question.

## Binding inputs and scope

Read master architecture, build-n-test, binding R2 sections 0-4 and 6,
both codex reviews, and spec section 7.5. Implemented only AL-2.
No AL-3 holder/reconfigure API or AL-4 trust commands introduced.
The initial report was written after the first implementation milestone
and updated after migration, stronger acceptance, mutation and lane gates.

## Files changed

- src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/interpreter.cljc: make mints one value; only a
  signed-name source gets admission state and an optional interpreter.
  round drains once, serves requests to the first pending, then serves
  the interpreter; it always returns the successor. Matched drains count
  as progress. Existing serve remains callable. retire preserves the
  whole value while retiring requests and forgetting their questions.
- src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc: one :linker session value; :link-source stays
  config and is supplied to each round. One recheck-on-tick hook retains
  the successor before driving the VM. Initial progress runs the VM
  before another round, within link-round-budget. Raises and rollback
  carry ::linker. Abandonment uses one retire call. Old protocol hooks
  and admission state machinery removed.
- src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc: one tick hook and one text collection.
- src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc: tick hook name in its docstring.
- test/yin/vm/linker/admission_test.cljc: caller/state path migration;
  existing seam tests now use round; six new portable acceptance tests.
  DHT fixtures retain the pair already attached to the VM when attaching
  signed-name linker state. Existing assertions retained.
- test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc: session pair path migration.
- test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc: pair paths and tick hook migration.
- test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc: same caller migration.

No other user's untracked collab files were changed.

## Acceptance coverage

All names below are in yin.vm.linker.admission-test unless specified.

A: one-tick-hands-external-and-snapshot-progress-to-the-vm-test
B: tick-rollbacks-carry-the-entire-linker-successor-test
C: idle-tick-does-not-run-or-increment-checks-test
D: continuing-tick-progress-is-bounded-test
E: only-signed-name-sources-mint-admission-state-test
F: a-matched-drain-is-progress-before-a-load-responds-test

- (a) A, external case: require parks with one question; append allow;
  one tick completes with one response, no additional question or event.
  Existing a-late-answer-completes-the-require-with-no-typed-line-test
  also passes through the unified tick.
- (b) A, snapshot case: empty decision medium parks; append snapshot;
  one tick answers, then the driver's next round drains and responds.
  Existing an-answer-alone-is-progress-and-the-drive-continues-test
  now calls recheck-on-tick and passes.
- Initial VM run/drain assertions: A and B trace round/drain/live-root-run
  order, exactly one live root run before another round, exactly one
  drain per round. Trace uses ffi/maybe-run rather than redefining a
  protocol function. It excludes the output tokenizer's already halted
  VM run; the pending driver's live root run is the handoff contract.
- (c) B: external refusal, snapshot refusal, external allow/install error,
  and snapshot allow/install error all roll back. Refusals arrive as VM
  link errors. Whole successor equality plus explicit request, answer
  and question cursor, serial and settled-map checks prove state carry.
  Existing an-install-error-keeps-the-admission-it-settled-test also
  preserves serial advancement for the next require (P2-3).
- (d) C: no progress/event runs no VM and leaves :checks unchanged.
- Bound: D injects continuing progress and asserts exactly
  link-round-budget rounds and runs, with :checks still zero.
- Non-DHT sessions: E covers absent/local/remote content sources, no
  admission key/interpreter on creation or successor, and DHT attachment.
- Matched-answer-only progress: F drains an allow while load is pending;
  no response is appended, but progress is true and the answer retained.
  The next unchanged round is idle and preserves the successor.
- P1-2 starvation/gap/no irrelevant-answer checks: existing
  the-host-hook-drains-irrelevant-answers-without-a-re-check-test now
  exercises round, including 64 irrelevant answers followed by allow,
  capacity-4 eviction/recovery, and draining while no run is pending.
- F3/retirement: existing abandonment and late-answer tests pass through
  the one-value retire and unified tick paths, retaining all assertions.
- Layering: yin.vm.linker.layering-test passes. Source/test search finds
  no old hook/key consumers. Admission vocabulary in repl.cljc appears
  only in configuration, option documentation and pending display.

The tick first assocs the successor and node. Only if the resulting
state is value-equal to the original does it reuse the original identity,
retaining existing idle identity assertions without losing any cursor.

## Mutation audit

Exactly one mutation per mechanism, red once each, then reverted.
Every mutant exited 1 with assertion failures and zero errors.
After each restore, git diff for its file was byte-identical to the
pre-mutation diff. Logs: target/al2-mutations/*.log and summary.txt.

