| One drain | drain twice | A | 4 |
| Initial progress | tick passes false | A | 6 |
| Rollback successor | omit ::linker restore | B | 4 |
| Round bound | >= becomes > | D | 1 |
| Matched drain progress | matched? false | F | 1 |

## Lane/check results

- Targeted migrated admission/require/doc/layering JVM gate:
  49 tests, 441 assertions, zero failures/errors (/tmp/al2-target3.log).
- Initial five new acceptance tests: 5 tests, 94 assertions, zero
  failures/errors (/tmp/al2-new.log). Subsequent timing runs cover all
  six tests and the stronger fourth rollback case; all green.
- Final broad JVM quick command (foreground, approved socket access):
  clojure -M:test -e :slow -r '"'^(yin[.]vm|yin[.]repl|yang[.]python).*'"'
  2566 tests, 40495 assertions, zero failures/errors, exit 0.
  Log: /tmp/al2-broad-final.log. Includes linker, require, dht, serve,
  python-antlr and DHT import namespaces, with slow tests excluded.
- Final portable instrumentation timing rerun: all six tests green,
  maximum 3.356 s (rollback); others under 2.4 s. No new >=5 s test on
  this laptop, so no new slow tag/guard required.
  Log: /tmp/al2-timing-portable.log.
- Kondo all eight changed source/test files: zero errors/warnings.
  Final changed test instrumentation lint also zero errors/warnings.
- mise exec -- cljstyle check: repo-wide check reports 25 unrelated
  pre-existing formatting failures. Changed-file check passes, as does
  final changed test check after the instrumentation adjustment.
- git diff --check passes. Added source/test lines are ASCII and <=80.

## Environment issues and remaining gates

Generated Python parser classes were initially absent. bb gen:python-antlr
completed with approved network escalation for the pinned inputs. The
initial sandboxed broad run stopped because local socket bind is denied;
its socket errors are environmental, and the identical socket-enabled
